  "description": "BEPKUD crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P b c n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C184 H232 O72 S16 Sm8,11(C2 H6 O1),6(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Sm1 (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm2 (Sm) has 9 O neighbors; Sm3 (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm4 (Sm) has 9 O neighbors; Sm4C (Sm) has 9 O neighbors; Sm1C (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm3C (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm2C (Sm) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 8 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.723-4.040 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 93.52-113.11°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C206H310O89S16Sm8. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
